          <p>
            <strong>Output derate.</strong> Natural gas carries less energy per unit volume to the cylinder than gasoline, so peak output drops roughly 20-25%. A generator rated 13,000 peak watts on gasoline delivers around 10,000 on natural gas. Standby units are rated on gas from the start, so this only matters when converting a portable.
          </p>
          <p>
