          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Choose Standby If...</h3>
          <p>
            You travel, or the house is often empty during the day. Someone in the household depends on powered medical equipment. You have a sump pump and a basement worth protecting when nobody is home. Or you simply want the outage to be a non-event rather than a task.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Choose a Portable If...</h3>
          <p>
            Someone is nearly always home. Outages are frequent enough to justify backup but not so severe that a fifteen-minute delay matters. You want the option to take the generator elsewhere on gasoline. Or the budget simply does not stretch to a standby installation — in which case a tri-fuel portable plumbed to gas delivers most of the practical benefit for a fifth of the cost.
          </p>
